\section{Symmetric stencil ledger}
For a declared positive step $h$, the author defines $d_h$ as the central-difference derivative approximation using the two displayed function values. All quantities use the same scalar coordinate.
\[
d_h=\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}
\]

\section{Macro-backed diffusion record}
\newcommand{\flux}{j}
The reviewed transport model declares the transparent macro below to expand to the flux symbol $j$. It adopts Fick diffusion, binds $D$ as diffusivity and $c$ as concentration, and declares the transport model for this region.
\[
\flux=-D\nabla c
\]

\section{Garnet probability model}
The model explicitly places events $C_g$ and $D_g$ in one probability space and records $P(D_g)>0$. It adopts the conditional probability identity
\[
P(C_g\mid D_g)=\frac{P(C_g\cap D_g)}{P(D_g)}
\]
The denominator guard and common-space declaration both apply to this display.
